{
  "title": "Coupling-modulated ring, 106.25 GBd PAM4 flow",
  "group": "Lasers & modulators",
  "description": "Example 47's coupling-modulated ring at 106.25 GBd PAM4 with realistic O-band PN and driver assumptions (junction RC through the driver and series resistance) and a four-step flow: find the resonance at the drive bias, PAM4 eye, optimize detuning / bias / arm imbalance / PN length / ring length for the worst spec margin, evaluate over a full PRBS-13Q period against RLM > 0.95, TDECQ < 1.5 dB, relOMA > -2 dB, ER > 3.5 dB. The flow shows the spec is out of reach for a lumped junction at 2 Vpp",
  "schematic": {
    "notes": [
      {
        "x": 40,
        "y": -360,
        "title": "Coupling-modulated ring at 106.25 GBd — a testbench flow",
        "lines": [
          "Example 47's ring at 106.25 GBd PAM4 with realistic drive and",
          "PN assumptions, all flow variables (Flow card -> vars):",
          "O-band lateral PN: VpiL 2.0 V*cm, 12 dB/cm, Cj0 0.3 fF/um,",
          "series R 10 Ohm*mm; driver 50 Ohm, 2 Vpp, 5 ps edges, 0.02 UI",
          "RJ/SJ/DJ. RDRV = driver + PN series R, so the junction RC",
          "limits bandwidth (example 47 drives the junctions ideally).",
          "1 Find resonance at the drive bias (1 nm sweep, > one FSR).",
          "2 PAM4 eye, 1000 symbols: rlm, er_db, rel_oma_db, il_db, tdecq_db.",
          "3 Optimize detune, bias, arm imbalance, PN and ring length for",
          "  the worst normalized spec margin, re-running 1 + 2 each time.",
          "4 Evaluate the optimum over a full PRBS-13Q period against",
          "  RLM > 0.95, TDECQ < 1.5 dB, relOMA > -2 dB, ER > 3.5 dB.",
          "Verdict: NOT met. At 2 Vpp the static levels cap relOMA near",
          "-3 dB (600 um PN); the RC (~25 GHz at 300 um, 50 Ohm) costs",
          "1.5-4 dB of TDECQ, so length trades OMA for TDECQ: about",
          "-5 dB relOMA at 3.5 dB TDECQ. Still optimistic: quasi-static",
          "optics (no photon lifetime; Q 1e4-1e5 is 10-60 ps vs 9.4 ps UI)."
        ]
      }
    ],
